FUNCTION FC 156 : VOID
TITLE =Banner Auto-Trim Interface
//DRAFT -- minimal skeleton, much less grounded than FC155/FC160. See
//FC156_design.md: this assumes the simplest possible interface (one
//discrete fault contact) purely as a placeholder to extend once
//Banner Auto-Trim's real interface (discrete/analog/serial) is known.
//If it turns out to need analog or serial data, this draft's shape is
//wrong and needs rebuilding, not just address changes.
//
//PLACEHOLDER: I 4.0 stands in for wherever Banner Auto-Trim's fault
//contact actually lands in HW Config. Polarity (active high/low) is
//also unconfirmed -- this assumes active-high (contact closed = fault).
//
//Call from OB1, alongside FC155 -- if this is a QC-relevant fault it
//belongs on the main scan, not FC160's relaxed OB35 cycle.

BEGIN

NETWORK
TITLE =Relay Banner Auto-Trim's fault contact into HMI DB10
      U     I     4.0                //BannerAutoTrim_FaultInput -- PLACEHOLDER address/polarity
      =     DB10.DBX   8.1           //BannerAutoTrimFault (already reserved by FC160's draft)

END_FUNCTION
